## Why This Is Asked
Assess foundational iOS accessibility and localization skills through a practical SwiftUI implementation. This verifies understanding of SwiftUI modifiers, data modeling with Codable, and basic persistence patterns.

## Key Concepts
- **Accessibility**: Labels, hints, large hit targets (44x44pt minimum), and dynamic type support
- **Localization**: LocalizedStringKey, locale configuration, and locale-aware date formatting
- **Persistence**: Codable encoding/decoding to JSON in the Documents directory
- **Data Model**: Task struct with title (String), dueDate (Date), and isCompleted (Bool)

## Implementation Sketch
```swift
struct Task: Codable, Identifiable {
    let id: UUID
    var title: String
    var dueDate: Date
    var isCompleted: Bool
}

@Observable
class TasksModel {
    var tasks: [Task] = []
    private let savePath = URL.documentsDirectory.appendingPathComponent("tasks.json")

    func save() throws { /* encode and write to savePath */ }
    func load() throws { /* decode from savePath */ }
}

struct ContentView: View {
    @State var model = TasksModel()
    var body: some View {
        List($model.tasks) { $task in
            TaskRow(task: $task)
                .accessibilityLabel(task.title)
                .accessibilityHint("Due \(task.dueDate, style: .relative) days")
                .accessibilityValue(task.isCompleted ? "Completed" : "Pending")
        }.font(.body) // dynamic type support
    }
}
```

## Test Plan
**Accessibility Tests:**
- Verify VoiceOver reads each task with label, due date, and completion status
- Confirm Dynamic Type scales UI correctly without truncation
- Ensure tap targets meet 44x44pt minimum

**Localization Tests:**
- Test date formatting across en, es, fr locales
- Verify all strings display correctly in each language
- Confirm layout accommodates varying string lengths

**Persistence Tests:**
- Save and reload tasks; verify data integrity
- Test edge cases: empty list, maximum tasks, corrupted file

